Package: nciusual
Title: NCI Method for Estimating Usual Dietary Intake Distributions
Version: 0.5.0
Authors@R: person("Conor", "McGovern", email = "comcgovern@example.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: R port of the National Cancer Institute (NCI) MIXTRAN, DISTRIB,
    and INDIVINT SAS macros (v2.1) for estimating usual dietary intake
    distributions from 24-hour dietary recall data. Fits amount-only models
    (for ubiquitously consumed nutrients) and uncorrelated/correlated two-part
    models (for episodically consumed foods) by survey-weighted maximum
    likelihood with the Box-Cox parameter estimated, as MIXTRAN does with PROC
    NLMIXED; simulates usual intake as DISTRIB does (9-point back-transformation
    over within-person error, weekday/weekend averaging); and predicts
    individual usual intake as INDIVINT does (conditional expectation by
    adaptive Gauss-Hermite quadrature). Also provides BRR standard errors,
    NHANES multi-cycle weight pooling, an approximate bivariate extension, and
    Gauss-Hermite quadrature utilities.
